@@host: Alaric died before the end of that year, four hundred and ten. He was perhaps forty years old. The river Busento still runs beneath the walls of Cosenza, in Calabria. His grave has never been found.

@@host: Sixty-six years later, the last emperor of the West, a boy named Romulus, was quietly deposed, and sent to live out his days in a villa near Naples. Nobody marked the moment as an ending. The city went on. The bells of its churches still ring today.

